ture"},{"type":"text_delta","text":".com/articles/s41"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"598-025-32673-9"},{"type":"text_delta","text":")\n\n**Ca"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"veats:**\n- Most"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" trials are"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" small, short"},{"type":"text_delta","text":","},{"type":"text_delta","text":" and at"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" some"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" risk of bias. Particip"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ants often don"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"'t st"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ick to the sch"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"edule.\n- Some pop"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ular s"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ources claim 5 to "},{"type":"text_delta","text":"10 mmHg drops"},{"type":"text_delta","text":". The"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" peer-reviewed stud"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ies above"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" don"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"'t support that range for"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" typ"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ical fasting prot"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ocols."},{"type":"text_delta","text":" [Superpower](https://"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"superpower.com/guides"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"/heart-cardiov"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ascular-testing/does-"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"fasting-raise-bl"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ood-pressure)\n-"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" I"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" haven't found long"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"-term data on wh"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ether fasting re"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"duces he"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"art attacks or str"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"okes.\n- If you take"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" bl"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ood pressure medication, f"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"asting can change"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" read"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ings and d"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"osing need"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"s, so tal"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"k to your doctor before star"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ting,"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" and"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" don"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"'t stop medication on"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" your own."},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"**Short answer:** Recent evidence suggests intermittent fasting (mainly time-restricted eating) may lower blood pressure modestly, but the effects are small, the trials are short, and results are inconsistent.\n\n- **Time-restricted eating without calorie cuts (2025 meta-analysis of 11 RCTs, 653 adults):** Systolic pressure fell by about 1.8 mmHg and diastolic by about 1.8 mmHg versus unrestricted eating. Larger drops appeared in people who started with high blood pressure. Heart rate also dropped slightly. The trials ran 6 to 52 weeks with eating windows of 6 to 10 hours. [Frontiers in Nutrition](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/nutrition/articles/10.3389/fnut.2025.1631477/full)\n- **Earlier meta-analysis (2022, 10 RCTs, 694 patients):** Time-restricted eating reduced systolic pressure by about 4 mmHg. The diastolic effect was not statistically significant. [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9644535)\n- **Women with overweight or obesity (2026 systematic review, 22 RCTs, 1,287 women):** Fasting improved BMI and fasting glucose, but the authors found no significant effect on blood pressure. [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42221756)\n- **Calorie-matched comparisons:** A 2023 meta-analysis found time-restricted eating did not beat calorie restriction for blood pressure, so any benefit may come mostly from eating less. [Eur J Clin Nutr](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41430-023-01311-w)\n- **5:2 diet (Scientific Reports, December 2025):** In a 12-week registry-based study of adults with overweight or obesity, the 5:2 diet was associated with greater systolic and pulse pressure improvement than some comparisons. The authors called the effect modest and asked for longer follow-up. [Scientific Reports](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-32673-9)\n\n**Caveats:**\n- Most trials are small, short, and at some risk of bias. Participants often don't stick to the schedule.\n- Some popular sources claim 5 to 10 mmHg drops. The peer-reviewed studies above don't support that range for typical fasting protocols. [Superpower](https://superpower.com/guides/heart-cardiovascular-testing/does-fasting-raise-blood-pressure)\n- I haven't found long-term data on whether fasting reduces heart attacks or strokes.\n- If you take blood pressure medication, fasting can change readings and dosing needs, so talk to your doctor before starting, and don't stop medication on your own."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1207,"cache_read_input_tokens":9905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7950},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
